# ================================================================
# LEAF-SWAB eDNA | PCoA OF VERTEBRATE COMMUNITY COMPOSITION
# ================================================================
# PURPOSE
#   A. Compare sampling heights using individual leaf-swab samples.
#   B. Compare locations after combining the three heights per plot.
#
# DATA AND TRANSFORMATION
#   OTU read counts -> curated taxa -> presence/absence (0/1).
#   Sørensen dissimilarity is calculated directly from binary data
#   using vegan::vegdist(comm, method = "bray", binary = TRUE).
#   Do NOT apply Hellinger transformation before this calculation.
#   PCoA uses a Cailliez additive correction where necessary.
#   PERMANOVA and dispersion retain the original Sørensen distances.
#
# STATISTICAL DESIGN
#   Height: permutations constrained within plot (repeated samples).
#   Location: one pooled presence/absence observation per plot.
#   PERMANOVA and dispersion test are distinct: check both results.
#   Envfit: height permutations constrained within plots; location unrestricted.
#   Envfit vectors are descriptive correlations, not causal effects.
#
# INPUT FILES (in working directory)
#   Combined_12S_read_table.xlsx
#   Combined_16S_read_table.xlsx
#   Sample names expected: LOCATION_HEIGHT_PLOT (e.g. SWN_Lower_01).
#
# OUTPUT DIRECTORY: figures5
#   Individual and combined plots in PNG and PDF formats.
#   PERMANOVA, dispersion and envfit summaries in CSV format.
#   All output files are created only when the script runs with input data.
# ================================================================

